\p{\strong{11:28 AM}}
\hr

\p{\em{Todays [[hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999]]}. Mainly about propositional logic, and the one formalized way of ensuring truth. The key observation is that at some level we must take a \em{leap of faith} and assume something is true in order to prove things.}
\ul{
\li{In order to avoid any associations or biases towards these assumptions, propositional logic simply abstracts these assumptions into atoms.}
\li{The notion of recursion and the snowballing of complexity also fits in through the meta-hiearchy of their \em{if-then} operator.}
}

